@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.TeamArdisaModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Ardisa Faras Dewi";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <!-- BACK -->
        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team">← Back</a>
        </div>

        <!-- HERO -->
        <div class="event-hero reveal">
            <div class="event-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Our Team</p>
                <h2>Ardisa Faras Dewi</h2>

                <p class="event-intro">
                    A Deaf barista whose journey with Kopi Cinta began from a simple wish
                    to work and gain new experience, then slowly grew into something more
                    meaningful through learning, adaptation, and belonging.
                </p>

                <div class="event-tags">
                    <span>Deaf Barista</span>
                    <span>Growth</span>
                    <span>Communication Access</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="team-profile-hero-img reveal">
                <img src="/images/team/ardisa.jpg" alt="Ardisa Faras Dewi">
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STORY -->
        <div class="hbii-block reveal">
            <div class="hbii-block-text">
                <p class="hbii-label">Her Beginning</p>
                <h3>Starting with a Simple Intention</h3>

                <p>
                    Ardisa’s journey with Kopi Cinta began from a simple intention:
                    to work and gain new experience.
                </p>

                <p>
                    She started by joining barista training for around two weeks,
                    learning from the very basics until she could understand the process more deeply.
                </p>

                <p>
                    After that, she continued as part of the team,
                    working behind the bar and also helping in the popcorn section.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-block-card">
                <h4>Her Role</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Deaf barista</li>
                    <li>Bar service</li>
                    <li>Popcorn station</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- GROWTH + COMFORT -->
        <div class="hbii-feature reveal">
            <div class="hbii-feature-card">
                <p class="hbii-label">Growth</p>
                <h3>Learning More Than Just Work</h3>

                <p>
                    At first, Ardisa wanted to understand the world of work and business—
                    learning SOPs, following recipes correctly, and getting familiar with
                    a more structured workflow.
                </p>

                <p>
                    But as time went on, she found something more than just a job.
                    She found a process that helped her keep learning and growing.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-feature-card soft">
                <p class="hbii-label">Comfort</p>
                <h3>Becoming Part of Something Meaningful</h3>

                <p>
                    For Ardisa, working at Kopi Cinta feels comfortable.
                    Even though there are tiring moments, she still goes through them happily,
                    because she feels that she is part of something meaningful.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- CHALLENGE -->
        <div class="hbii-block reveal">
            <div class="hbii-block-text">
                <p class="hbii-label">Challenge</p>
                <h3>When Communication Takes More Effort</h3>

                <p>
                    One of the biggest challenges Ardisa faces is communication
                    with hearing people.
                </p>

                <p>
                    She often relies on lip-reading, which can become difficult
                    when someone speaks too quickly.
                </p>

                <p>
                    But through those moments, she continues to adapt, learn, and grow.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-highlight-panel">
                <div>
                    <strong>Writing</strong>
                    <span>Helps make meaning clearer.</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Gestures</strong>
                    <span>Can support everyday understanding.</span>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Sign Language</strong>
                    <span>Creates more equal communication access.</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- MESSAGE -->
        <div class="hbii-ending reveal">
            <h3>Her Hope</h3>
            <p>
                Through her journey, Ardisa hopes hearing people can become more aware
                of how important communication access is for Deaf individuals—
                whether through writing, gestures, or sign language.
            </p>
            <p>
                Because for her, access is not just about understanding words,
                but about making sure no one is left out of the conversation.
            </p>
        </div>
        <br />
        <!-- BACK -->
        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Team</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>